    bodyHtml:
      '<div class="jumbotron dark-sections">\n           <div class="container">\n             <h1><span class="brand-blue">Panel Discussion: HK Education and Python</span></h1>\n             <h2>Moderator: Haggen So</h2>\n             <p>Language: Cantonese</p>\n           </div>\n         </div>\n\n        <div class="container">\n          <div class="row">\n            <div class="col-sm-3">\n              <h3>Moderator</h3>\n              <h4>Dr. Haggen So</h4>\n              <img src="/2016/remote/img.opensource.hk/haggen.jpg" alt="Photo of Dr. Haggen So" class="img-thumbnail">\n            </div>\n            <div class="col-sm-9">\n              <h3>Tentative List of Panellists (in alphabetical order)</h3>\n              <table class="table table-striped table-bordered">\n                <tr>\n                  <td>\n                  Albert Kin Wai WONG, Chairman of Aitle(Association of I.T. Leaders in Education 資訊科技教育領袖協會)\n                  <br />\n                  <a href="http://www.aitle.org.hk/" target="_blank">http://www.aitle.org.hk/</a> - Primary and Secondary Education in Hong Kong\n                  </td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <td>\n                  Isaac Li, student from First Code Academy, speaker at PyCon Taiwan 2016 <br/>\n                   <a href="https://tw.pycon.org/2016/en-us/events/talk/52458110886871052/" target="_blank">\n                     https://tw.pycon.org/2016/en-us/events/talk/52458110886871052/</a> - First person experience in Python\n                </td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <td>\n                  Kenneth Kin Pong Kwok, Assistant Marketing Manager of Koding Kingdom,\n                  <a href="https://www.kodingkingdom.com/home/?page_id=71" target="_blank"><br />\n                    https://www.kodingkingdom.com/home/?page_id=71</a> – Python and Coding Courses in Hong Kong\n                  </td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <td>\n                  Dr. Dennis Y. W. Liu, Teaching Fellow at the Department of Computing of The Hong Kong Polytechnic University\n                  <br/>\n                  <a href="http://www4.comp.polyu.edu.hk/~csdennis/" target="_blank"> http://www4.comp.polyu.edu.hk/~csdennis/</a>- Tertiary Education in Hong Kong\n                  </td>\n                </tr>\n              </table>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n          <div class="row">\n            <div class="col-sm-12">\n              <h3>About the Discussion</h3>\n              <p class="topic"> The Python programming language is widely employed for education purpose around the\n                world. Is Python also relevant to education in Hong Kong? A number of panellists from different\n                backgrounds are invited to the discussion.</p>\n              <p>Tags: Python, Education</p>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n          <hr />\n\n        <footer>\n          <p>PyCon HK 2016 Committee</p>\n        </footer>\n      </div>\n    </div>',
    visibleText:
      'Panel Discussion: HK Education and Python Moderator: Haggen So Language: Cantonese Moderator Dr. Haggen So Tentative List of Panellists (in alphabetical order) Albert Kin Wai WONG, Chairman of Aitle(Association of I.T. Leaders in Education 資訊科技教育領袖協會) http://www.aitle.org.hk/ - Primary and Secondary Education in Hong Kong Isaac Li, student from First Code Academy, speaker at PyCon Taiwan 2016 https://tw.pycon.org/2016/en-us/events/talk/52458110886871052/ - First person experience in Python Kenneth Kin Pong Kwok, Assistant Marketing Manager of Koding Kingdom, https://www.kodingkingdom.com/home/?page_id=71 – Python and Coding Courses in Hong Kong Dr. Dennis Y. W. Liu, Teaching Fellow at the Department of Computing of The Hong Kong Polytechnic University http://www4.comp.polyu.edu.hk/~csdennis/ - Tertiary Education in Hong Kong About the Discussion The Python programming language is widely employed for education purpose around the world. Is Python also relevant to education in Hong Kong? A number of panellists from different backgrounds are invited to the discussion. Tags: Python, Education PyCon HK 2016 Committee',
